    "title": "private broadcast: wait synchronously for mempool acceptance",
    "user": {
      "login": "andrewtoth",
      "id": 237213,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIzNzIxMw==",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/237213?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/andrewtoth",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andrewtoth/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Calling `BroadcastTransaction` with the `NO_MEMPOOL_PRIVATE_BROADCAST` method skips inserting the transaction into the mempool and returns immediately. This causes problems with software that expects the transaction to be in the mempool after the function returns. For example many third-party wallets or services call `sendrawtransaction` and expect the transaction to be in the mempool after it returns a successful response.\n\nThis PR adds a new `TransactionAddedToMempoolSync` method to `CValidationInterface`. This is then used in `BroadcastTransaction` when the method is `NO_MEMPOOL_PRIVATE_BROADCAST` to wait for the transaction to have been accepted back into the mempool before returning. It also adds a timeout (default 10 minutes) to `BroadcastTransaction` and exposes it as an option for `sendrawtransaction`. Setting the timeout to 0 disables the wait and returns immediately, preserving the current behavior.\n\nSynchronously waiting for mempool acceptance is also a prerequisite for adding private broadcast support to the wallet. The `TransactionAddedToMempoolSync` method is added specifically for future wallet broadcasting, so a broadcast caller holding `cs_wallet` will not timeout waiting on another background event that is also trying to acquire `cs_wallet`.",
