      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": ">  For example many third-party wallets or services call sendrawtransaction and expect the transaction to be in the mempool after it returns a successful response.\r\n\r\nCan we gather a list of these? \r\n\r\nGiven the Core wallet motivation in part I think I'd like to see end to end wallet integration before stepping through this change. Naively done, it could end up with some dangerous behavior for users, such as:\r\n\r\n - sendtoaddress hangs while Tor connects and the transaction travels out and back. Waits up to 10 minutes(?)\r\n - The user presses Ctrl-C. The transaction is already in the wallet and queued.\r\n - The user runs getbalance or listtransactions to check what happened. Both block on cs_wallet, so the user can't see that the first send went through. I think they'd have to inspect the private broadcast queue instead to know?\r\n - The user runs sendtoaddress again. It blocks on cs_wallet until the first call finishes. Then coin selection skips the now-spent inputs and builds a second transaction from other coins. Both get broadcast, and the user pays twice.\r\n\r\nsendtoaddress was never idempotent to begin with, which is kind of scary on its own, I just think this broadens the scope of possible loss through unclear UX. Users suddenly \"losing\" funds by stuff not being in mempool and not being accounted for will at least cause the users to slow down :/",
